<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>Talks — Olivia Sloth</title>
	</head>

	<body>
		<header>
			<a class="name" href="/">OLIVIA SLOTH</a>

			<nav>
				<a href="/stories">Stories</a>
				<a class="active" href="/talks">Talks</a>
				<a href="/about">About</a>
			</nav>
		</header>

		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<p class="eyebrow">TALKS</p>
				<h1>Two talks. Two different roads.</h1>

				<p class="intro">
					One about adventure, mountains and leaving the main road.
					The other about finding your own way through school, work and life.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="talks">

				<article class="talk-card">
					<div class="talk-image">
						<img src="/tur2.JPEG" alt="Olivia Sloth travelling in the mountains" />
					</div>

					<div class="talk-content">
						<p class="number">01</p>
						<p class="label">ADVENTURE & OUTDOOR</p>

						<h2>Off the main road</h2>

						<p class="subtitle">
							Solo hiking, mountains and slow travel through places we often associate with conflict.
						</p>

						<p>
							A talk about moving away from the obvious route — literally and otherwise.
							I share stories from solo journeys, outdoor life and time spent travelling slowly
							through countries that are often primarily known through conflict and headlines.
						</p>

						<p>
							It is about the people you meet when you stay longer, walk instead of drive,
							and allow plans to change along the way.
						</p>

						<p class="good-for">
							<strong>Good for:</strong> libraries, outdoor clubs, højskoler, associations,
							cultural venues and companies.
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>


				<article class="talk-card reverse">
					<div class="talk-image">
						<img src="/te_speak.JPEG" alt="Olivia Sloth giving a talk" />
					</div>

					<div class="talk-content">
						<p class="number">02</p>
						<p class="label">SCHOOLS & YOUNG PEOPLE</p>

						<h2>Choosing Curiosity Over the Fear of Failure</h2>

						<p class="subtitle">
							From struggling in school to a PhD in physics — and what happened when I became more curious than afraid of getting it wrong.
						</p>

						<p>
							I was never the obvious candidate for an academic career. School was difficult,
							and for a long time I did not think of myself as someone who belonged in that world.
						</p>

						<p>
							This talk is about learning differently, taking detours and eventually completing
							a PhD in physics — without suddenly becoming the person who always chooses the safe
							or expected route.
						</p>

						<p>
							The focus can be adapted to the age of the students and the setting.
						</p>

						<p class="good-for">
							<strong>Good for:</strong> schools, efterskoler, gymnasiums, højskoler
							and educational events.
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>

			</section>


			<section class="details">
				<div>
					<p class="label">FORMAT</p>
					<p>Talk, break and Q&A</p>
				</div>

				<div>
					<p class="label">LANGUAGE</p>
					<p>Danish or English</p>
				</div>

				<div>
					<p class="label">CUSTOM</p>
					<p>Both talks can be adapted to the audience and event.</p>
				</div>
			</section>


			<section class="booking">
				<p class="label">BOOK A TALK</p>

				<h2>Want me to come and speak?</h2>

				<p>
					Send me a message with a little about the audience, the event and which talk you are interested in.
				</p>

				<a href="mailto:YOUR-EMAIL-HERE">Get in touch →</a>
			</section>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>


